### SSA and memory, in one picture

```text
SSA result → store into an entry-allocated slot → load at a use
```

| Term | Meaning in these lessons |
| --- | --- |
| SSA | Static single assignment: each SSA value has one definition; definitions must satisfy dominance requirements at their uses. |
| Dominance | A definition’s block lies on every reachable path to a use’s block. New CFG edges can invalidate it. |
| PHI | An SSA merge selecting an incoming value according to the predecessor edge used to enter a block. |
| Demotion | Replace selected SSA value flow with stack storage, stores, and loads to prepare for CFG changes. |
| Stack slot / alloca | Storage allocated in the function’s stack frame; the alloca instruction returns a pointer to it. |
| load / store | Read a typed value from memory / write a value to memory. A store has no SSA result. |
| Void result | The instruction produces no value for another instruction to consume, regardless of its operand types. |
| Cross-block / escaping value | An instruction result used outside the block in which it was defined. “Escaping” here is not a full escape analysis. |
| Worklist | A C++ collection of pointers to instructions to process after discovery; it does not own those instructions. |
| isa / dyn_cast | LLVM type check returning bool / checked cast returning a typed pointer or nullptr. |
| Upcast / downcast | Treat a derived object as its base type / access a base-typed object through a more specific type after a valid check. |
| Iterator invalidation | A saved traversal position may stop being valid when its underlying instruction list is changed. |
| PreservedAnalyses | The pass’s report of which cached analysis results remain valid after it runs. |
| DenseMap | LLVM’s key/value container; here BasicBlock* keys map to unsigned IDs. Iteration order is not presentation order. |
| State ID | The integer naming a destination block in our dispatcher; not the same as the block’s optional printed name. |
| Dispatcher | A block loading the next state and switching to the corresponding original block. |
| Setup / entry | The preserved one-time function entry, holding allocations and initialization outside repeated state dispatch. |
| LLVMContext | LLVM’s shared context for IR facilities such as uniqued types; obtained here from the function. |
| IRBuilder | An LLVM helper that inserts instructions at a chosen position or at the end of a block. |
| Insertion point | The position where the builder will insert the next instruction; a pointer-based constructor can insert before an existing instruction. |
| getInt32Ty / getInt32 | Get the LLVM i32 Type / get an i32 ConstantInt holding a particular value. |
| Switch capacity / case | Reserved space is not an edge. addCase associates an integer constant with a destination block. |
| Terminator | The final instruction in a complete basic block; replacements must leave exactly one valid terminator. |
| unreachable | A terminator declaring that the path must not execute in a valid run; it is not recovery logic. |
| eraseFromParent | Remove and delete an instruction from its block. Do not use its pointer afterward. |
| Prototype checkpoint | A deliberately limited stage that can verify without implementing all supported input cases or full flattening. |

